# Implementation Patterns Rules

## Prefer Validated Patterns

When implementing or modifying Fast Mode parallel chunking:

- PREFER patterns validated in existing open-source tools
- PREFER established libraries (workerpool, Comlink) over custom solutions
- PREFER algorithms from reference implementations (OpenAI Whisper, WhisperX)
- AVOID "rolling your own" from scratch when proven patterns exist

## Required References

Before implementing parallel processing features, review:

1. **Transformers.js examples** - Worker wiring patterns
2. **workerpool API** - Task distribution, error recovery
3. **OpenAI Whisper transcribe.py** - Chunking algorithm, merging logic
4. **whisper.cpp** - Job queue model, progress reporting

## Attribution

Document pattern sources in code comments:

```typescript
// Pattern: Job queue with worker pool
// Source: Adapted from workerpool API + whisper.cpp scheduling
// Reference: https://github.com/josdejong/workerpool
```

## Chunking Algorithm Compliance

Chunk creation and merging MUST follow OpenAI Whisper spec:

- 30s chunks (configurable)
- Overlap to prevent word splitting (5s standard, 3s fast mode)
- Timestamp adjustment when merging
- Results stitched in order regardless of completion order

## Worker Pool Guidelines

When using workerpool or similar:

- Initialize pool once, reuse for all chunks
- Terminate pool after processing complete
- Handle worker crashes with re-queue to other workers
- Fall back to sequential if all workers fail

## Browser Adaptation

When adapting non-browser patterns:

- Replace threads with Web Workers
- Replace shared memory with transferable objects (Float32Array)
- Replace file I/O with Blob/ArrayBuffer handling
- Ensure all processing stays client-side (privacy rule)

## Knowledge Base Search

When exploring new patterns, search across:

- npm registry (npmjs.com)
- Code sandboxes (CodePen, StackBlitz, JSFiddle)
- Developer blogs and tutorials
- Academic/research demo sites
- NOT just GitHub
